This is a Rust workspace. Crates live in crates/; ui/ has the TypeScript/Electron UI.

crates (real list as of 2026-10-19):
- aegis: core logic (agents, providers, config, prompts, hints, session, checks)
- aegis-cli: the `aegis` binary and the terminal session UI
- aegis-agent: agent runtime pieces shared by the CLI and the server path
- aegis-providers + aegis-provider-types: provider implementations and wire types
- aegis-context-management: compaction, context window and tool-pair summarization
- aegis-mcp: bundled MCP servers; the developer subsystem lives here
- aegis-acp-macros, aegis-roaming, aegis-download-manager, aegis-local-inference,
  aegis-sdk, aegis-sdk-types, aegis-test, aegis-test-support
ui/: aegis-acp, aegis-acp-client, aegis-binary, desktop (Electron), text

There is NO aegis-server and NO aegis-bench crate in this fork. The HTTP/ACP server is the
`serve` subcommand of the `aegis` binary (crates/aegis-cli), not a separate crate; the
`aegisd` that runs on port 8765 belongs to the *bridge* project (C:\Aegis-Proyects\bridge).

Non-trivial features go in the aegis crate and are called from aegis-cli.

Builds on this machine:
- CARGO_TARGET_DIR=C:\Aegis-Proyects\target. src/target is NOT used anymore (fossil, removed 2026-10-19).
- Deploy: core/ops/build-and-swap.ps1 -Version vNN (build-safe + copy to core/bin + swap.ps1).
- Do not hardcode `-o src/target/...`; cargo already writes into C:\Aegis-Proyects\target.

tips:
- always check it compiles: cargo fmt, cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings, and the tests of the files you touched
- reduced CLI feature set: rustls-tls,scheduler,bundled-mcp,chat-recall,acp-http,code-mode
- CI feature set for the aegis lib suite: rustls-tls,code-mode,tree-sitter,live-voice,scheduler,platform-apps,chat-recall,acp-http
- unstaged changes are a good signal of what is being worked on
